  "worked_solution": "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
